    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d406">

                <pb facs="1355" n="1324" xml:id="pg1324"/>

                <head>406. Telegram From the Embassy in Czechoslovakia to the Department of
                        State<anchor n="1" xml:id="d406-f1"/></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#float-left">4584.</seg><dateline rendition="#float-right"
                            ><placeName> Prague</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1981-11-06">November 6, 1981, 1425Z</date></dateline></opener>
                <!--<pb facs="d406-2" n="2" type="facsimile" xml:id="d406-2"/>-->
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>Czechoslovak Claims Agreement.</item>
                </list>
                <p>Claims agreement was initialed November 6 by Charge and Director Kral of MFA legal office. Initialed English and Czech
                    texts will be pouched November 10 and should arrive Washington November 13.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold"
                            >Matlock</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d406-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d406-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Department of State, Central Foreign Policy File, D810527–1058.
                    Confidential; Immediate. Sent for information to Bern, Brussels, London, Paris,
                    and Zurich. The text of the claims agreement was sent to London on November 13
                    in telegram 302976. (Department of State, Central Foreign Policy File,
                    D810540–0471)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
